 "rendered": "<p>You are reading about QFWFQ, winner of Best Solo Show at the 2025 Hollywood Fringe. A surrealist labyrinth that stretches time and space. Inspired by Italo Calvino&#8217;s If On a Winter&#8217;s Night a Traveller, this razor-sharp, absurdly funny and deeply personal show breaks all genres and has no fourth wall.</p>\n<p>Join trans artist Gregory Nussen as they rummage through the power and peril of storytelling, growing up Jewish and queer, grappling with geopolitics, and art that saves your life.</p>\n<p>QFWFQ neither begins, nor ends. How does it come together? I can\u2019t explain, but it does.</p>\n<p>Directed by Hannah Pilkes.</p>\n",
 "protected": false
}

